From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ayman Ragab <aymanrar2c@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 07:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] soc: qcom: pdr: retry service lookup on transient
 failures

pdr_notify_lookup_failure() deleted the lookup entry on ANY non-ENXIO
error. A single QMI timeout during ADSP restart permanently removed
the sensor PD tracking entry, requiring a full re-initialization.

Fix by:
- Adding a lookup_retries counter to pdr_service
- Keeping the entry on transient errors and retrying up to
  PDR_LOOKUP_MAX_RETRIES (10) times
- Also treat -EAGAIN as a retryable error

Signed-off-by: Ayman Ragab <aymanrar2c@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/pdr_interface.c | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/pdr_interface.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/pdr_interface.c
index 72259f489075..24958171fbf1 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/pdr_interface.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/pdr_interface.c
@@ -29,6 +29,8 @@ struct pdr_service {
 	bool need_locator_lookup;
 	bool service_connected;
 
+	unsigned int lookup_retries;
+
 	struct list_head node;
 };
 
@@ -438,16 +440,25 @@ static int pdr_locate_service(struct pdr_handle *pdr, struct pdr_service *pds)
 	return ret;
 }
 
+#define PDR_LOOKUP_MAX_RETRIES	10
+
 static void pdr_notify_lookup_failure(struct pdr_handle *pdr,
 				      struct pdr_service *pds,
 				      int err)
 {
-	pr_err("PDR: service lookup for %s failed: %d\n",
-	       pds->service_name, err);
+	pr_err("PDR: service lookup for %s failed: %d (retry %u)\n",
+	       pds->service_name, err, pds->lookup_retries);
 
-	if (err == -ENXIO)
+	if (err == -ENXIO || err == -EAGAIN)
 		return;
 
+	pds->lookup_retries++;
+	if (pds->lookup_retries < PDR_LOOKUP_MAX_RETRIES)
+		return;
+
+	pr_err("PDR: service lookup for %s failed after %u retries, giving up\n",
+	       pds->service_name, pds->lookup_retries);
+
 	list_del(&pds->node);
 	pds->state = SERVREG_LOCATOR_ERR;
 	mutex_lock(&pdr->status_lock);
